{"diagnosis": "Loopback TX of 0xa5 was received as 0xff (idle) with TRAP uart data mismatch got 0xff want 0xa5. send_divcnt increments every clk but line 130 compares with (cfg_divider >> 4), giving ~6-cycle bit period for divider 64 instead of ~65 cycles. This 16x-too-fast TX breaks RX bit timing so the receiver misses the frame and stays idle.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@
 			send_bitcnt <= 10;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
-			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;", "expected": "tohost PASS 0x1, no TRAP, uart data got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

